# Backtest inference metrics (PSR / DSR)

When this rule attaches, wire trial-aware inference through the canonical modules — never hand-roll PSR or DSR in notebooks.

## Canonical modules

| Need | Module / API |
|------|----------------|
| PSR / DSR math | `09_performance/sharpe_inference.py` — `probabilistic_sharpe_ratio`, `deflated_sharpe_ratio` |
| Net metrics + inference | `05_strategies/s2_coint/metrics.py` — `metrics_from_returns_inference` |
| S2 backtest runner | `04_backtest/s2_coint/runner.py` — `run_s2_backtest` (`n_trials_local`, `n_trials_stack`) |
| Fold-val / selection tables | `04_backtest/s2_coint/report.py` — `fold_val_metrics`, `full_is_metrics`, `arm_selection_table` |
| Trial ledger | `04_backtest/s2_coint/research.py` — `register_hypothesis_arms`, `n_trials_local`, `n_trials_stack` |
| Interpretation | `05_strategies/s2_coint/s2_algorithm_notes.md` — PSR/DSR + ledger only |

## S2 hypothesis notebook pattern

```python
from backtest.s2_coint.research import register_hypothesis_arms, n_trials_local, n_trials_stack

register_hypothesis_arms("H-009", list(configs.keys()), overwrite=True)
fold_df = fold_val_metrics(panel, folds, configs, hyp_id="H-009", s1_weekly=s1_weekly)
full_is_df = full_is_metrics(panel, configs, hyp_id="H-009", s1_weekly=s1_weekly)
display(arm_selection_table(fold_df, full_is_df))
# STAR selection stays manual; rank hints use median_val_sharpe only
```

## Rules

1. Every arm screen must call `register_hypothesis_arms` before scoring (update ledger when pre-registered arms add/remove).
2. Use `fold_val_metrics(..., hyp_id=...)` and `full_is_metrics(..., hyp_id=...)` so rows include `ann_sharpe`, `max_drawdown`, `corr_to_s1`, `psr`, `dsr_local`, `dsr_stack`, `n_trials_local`, `n_trials_stack`, `n_days`.
3. Display `arm_selection_table(fold_df, full_is_df)` — keep `max_drawdown` and `corr_to_s1`; no programmatic winner column.
4. When extending `04_backtest/` metrics code, use `metrics_from_returns_inference`; do not drop co-primary columns.
5. STAR / ranking stays on median val `ann_sharpe` (Option 4); PSR/DSR are diagnostic only.
6. Sealed OOS tearsheets: pass trial counts into `write_tearsheet_pdf` when reporting stack DSR.

See also: `.cursor/rules/research-validation-bias.mdc` (validation discipline); `05_strategies/s2_coint/s2_algorithm_notes.md` for metric interpretation.
